1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:01,790
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,793 --> 00:00:02,981
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:05,427
(Episode 27)

4
00:00:12,059 --> 00:00:13,971
Cook the egg strips properly.

5
00:00:14,430 --> 00:00:16,527
Hey, just do the dishes. I'll do it.

6
00:00:17,184 --> 00:00:18,977
This is harder than it looks.

7
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:23,175
That's hot!

8
00:00:23,177 --> 00:00:25,693
Don't let the water splash.
It'll splatter in the oil.

9
00:00:25,748 --> 00:00:27,576
Stop nagging me.

10
00:00:27,578 --> 00:00:30,107
You think I'm the pampered
eldest son like you?

11
00:00:30,110 --> 00:00:32,917
Mom always treated you like her husband,

12
00:00:32,919 --> 00:00:34,211
always doting on you.

13
00:00:34,278 --> 00:00:37,243
And you? You acted like royalty
every time you were sick.

14
00:00:37,870 --> 00:00:38,923
That's true.

15
00:00:40,118 --> 00:00:41,390
The pampered eldest son...

16
00:00:41,845 --> 00:00:44,001
This time, everything came to light.

17
00:00:46,375 --> 00:00:47,735
Stop saying that.

18
00:00:47,942 --> 00:00:49,355
We all understand.

19
00:00:49,462 --> 00:00:51,500
Parents always love their children more.

20
00:00:52,536 --> 00:00:53,536
Didn't you know?

21
00:00:53,824 --> 00:00:55,176
Hey, you're dripping water.

22
00:00:57,836 --> 00:01:00,517
- I'm done.
- Me too. Let's roll them now.

23
00:01:10,970 --> 00:01:13,596
- Hey, just put in a little rice.
- I know.

24
00:01:13,643 --> 00:01:15,238
You nag like an old man.

25
00:01:17,664 --> 00:01:21,249
Remember when we were kids?
You said you'd make mom seaweed soup...

26
00:01:21,384 --> 00:01:23,201
for her birthday, but you knocked it over?

27
00:01:23,243 --> 00:01:25,050
That was because of you too.

28
00:01:25,052 --> 00:01:26,690
Everything's always my fault!

29
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:29,830
That's why you're such
a typical Korean eldest son.

30
00:01:29,832 --> 00:01:30,973
Let's drop it.

31
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:33,940
Here.

32
00:01:40,790 --> 00:01:42,696
- It's delicious.
- It's delicious.

33
00:01:47,453 --> 00:01:48,552
What are you doing?

34
00:01:50,790 --> 00:01:54,097
Don't play with your food.

35
00:01:54,203 --> 00:01:55,609
We're not playing.

36
00:01:55,765 --> 00:01:59,240
Don't disrespect
the brotherhood of gimbap. Have a taste.

37
00:02:01,596 --> 00:02:02,920
It's delicious.

38
00:02:03,596 --> 00:02:06,279
- What's the occasion?
- O Reum's getting discharged.

39
00:02:06,653 --> 00:02:09,013
You and mom have been through
so much lately,

40
00:02:09,356 --> 00:02:11,309
so we wanted to make you
at least one meal.

41
00:02:12,481 --> 00:02:14,021
That's my husband.

42
00:02:18,156 --> 00:02:20,089
Mai, I helped too.

43
00:02:20,177 --> 00:02:21,824
Just focus on your dating life.

44
00:02:22,051 --> 00:02:23,386
And open your eyes for once.

45
00:02:23,512 --> 00:02:26,174
- "Open your eyes for once."
- Seriously!

46
00:02:31,596 --> 00:02:33,937
- Roll it properly.
- Isn't this right?

47
00:02:36,295 --> 00:02:39,441
- Really?
- Yeah. Go wash up and come back.

48
00:02:39,731 --> 00:02:41,920
Seung Woo made egg soup too.

49
00:02:43,323 --> 00:02:44,506
Let's eat.

50
00:02:46,788 --> 00:02:48,340
I feel like I've been hit by a truck.

51
00:02:50,532 --> 00:02:52,266
Of course you do.

52
00:02:52,358 --> 00:02:54,010
You've been through so much.

53
00:02:54,847 --> 00:02:58,021
Once O Reum comes home,
there'll be so much to do.

54
00:03:03,506 --> 00:03:05,100
Poor mother.

55
00:03:12,892 --> 00:03:15,429
You two got up at dawn and made all this?

56
00:03:15,432 --> 00:03:17,706
For my Yeong Ju.

57
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:20,329
For my sweet Mai.

58
00:03:22,758 --> 00:03:25,099
- Let's eat, Mai.
- Yeah, Mother.

59
00:03:27,832 --> 00:03:29,210
- Mother.
- Yeah?

60
00:03:29,285 --> 00:03:31,417
- Open up.
- Okay.

61
00:03:33,558 --> 00:03:34,961
Thank you.

62
00:03:35,152 --> 00:03:38,501
I'd have been so lost without you.
I might've died.

63
00:03:38,611 --> 00:03:39,664
Hey!

64
00:03:39,811 --> 00:03:42,667
Don't say you're going to die
when you have a child. Didn't you see?

65
00:03:42,737 --> 00:03:44,998
I know. I won't. Shh.

66
00:03:46,346 --> 00:03:49,031
I always wished I had a daughter,

67
00:03:49,165 --> 00:03:50,447
but sons are better.

68
00:03:50,450 --> 00:03:52,136
Now that I think about it,
daughters really are something.

69
00:03:52,843 --> 00:03:54,936
How can she be so harsh?

70
00:03:56,333 --> 00:03:58,998
- I still like having a daughter.
- No way.

71
00:03:59,512 --> 00:04:01,399
I'm glad O Reum is a boy.

72
00:04:01,664 --> 00:04:03,042
Daughters scare me.

73
00:04:04,502 --> 00:04:06,323
But she'll be okay, right?

74
00:04:06,950 --> 00:04:08,262
She needs to build her strength back up.

75
00:04:08,948 --> 00:04:10,245
Don't worry.

76
00:04:10,392 --> 00:04:13,188
She left saying she never wanted
to see us again. Why worry about her?

77
00:04:14,027 --> 00:04:15,600
I was about to say,

78
00:04:16,049 --> 00:04:19,487
"I can't thank you enough,"
I had to bite my tongue.

79
00:04:19,550 --> 00:04:21,935
Still, we have to look out for Ji Ni.

80
00:04:22,372 --> 00:04:24,626
I can't help thinking of her
whenever I see O Reum.

81
00:04:24,725 --> 00:04:25,755
Exactly.

82
00:04:26,092 --> 00:04:28,212
We shouldn't forget what she did for us.

83
00:04:42,716 --> 00:04:44,360
Eat something before you go.

84
00:04:44,363 --> 00:04:45,834
Don't worry about me.

85
00:04:47,428 --> 00:04:48,746
Seriously!

86
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:51,581
Dad told you to take good care of me.
That was his dying wish.

87
00:04:51,584 --> 00:04:53,967
Getting rid of this stuff
is how I take care of you.

88
00:04:56,022 --> 00:04:58,308
- Are you getting rid of it? Or should I?
- Leave it.

89
00:04:58,371 --> 00:05:00,194
What did the wine ever do to you?

90
00:05:00,196 --> 00:05:02,166
It does plenty.

91
00:05:02,169 --> 00:05:03,548
It puts you in danger.

92
00:05:03,668 --> 00:05:06,813
Your stomach's already in bad shape.
Should you really be drinking again?

93
00:05:06,890 --> 00:05:09,449
I'm not drinking now.
I'll drink it later, so leave it.

94
00:05:13,441 --> 00:05:14,506
Na Ji Ni!

95
00:05:18,388 --> 00:05:20,081
What a waste!

96
00:05:21,685 --> 00:05:24,055
I know every bottle of alcohol
in this house,

97
00:05:24,057 --> 00:05:25,973
so don't touch any of it
for at least a year.

98
00:05:26,270 --> 00:05:28,887
- It's expensive.
- More expensive than you?

99
00:05:29,049 --> 00:05:30,438
Are you okay with me being an orphan?

100
00:05:37,912 --> 00:05:39,126
Stop right there.

101
00:05:40,368 --> 00:05:41,368
What?

102
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:42,590
Do you still have something to say?

103
00:05:42,628 --> 00:05:45,192
I think you've forgotten
why I tried to kill myself.

104
00:05:45,290 --> 00:05:48,333
You think I hated the world?
It was because of you.

105
00:05:48,430 --> 00:05:51,275
You betrayed me, then sat there
laughing with the Seo Chon family.

106
00:05:51,710 --> 00:05:54,733
- How could I live after seeing that?
- I apologized.

107
00:05:54,830 --> 00:05:57,870
And you said it was the right thing to do,
that it was a good thing.

108
00:06:01,012 --> 00:06:02,152
You wrote it right here.

109
00:06:02,220 --> 00:06:04,617
You wrote this, right?
You have nothing to say, right?

110
00:06:06,026 --> 00:06:07,913
It's barely been any time
since dad passed away.

111
00:06:08,056 --> 00:06:09,832
Do I really have to read your will?

112
00:06:10,850 --> 00:06:13,635
- Why do you carry this around?
- I want to keep it.

113
00:06:19,057 --> 00:06:20,232
You little brat.

114
00:06:30,510 --> 00:06:32,274
We're still on for today, right?

115
00:06:33,281 --> 00:06:34,281
Yes.

116
00:06:49,024 --> 00:06:52,380
You want us to republish
a collection of Korean folktales,

117
00:06:52,691 --> 00:06:54,401
so I've put together some concepts.

118
00:06:54,948 --> 00:06:56,099
The drawings look different.

119
00:06:56,101 --> 00:06:58,357
I didn't know Korean art
could look like this.

120
00:06:58,550 --> 00:07:01,382
I learned that myself
while working with Ji Ni.

121
00:07:02,109 --> 00:07:03,740
Lately, at international art festivals,

122
00:07:03,742 --> 00:07:06,272
Korean folk art has been getting
a lot more attention.

123
00:07:06,412 --> 00:07:08,626
And as you know,
Korean animation has been a hit too.

124
00:07:08,735 --> 00:07:10,819
That's right. I was really surprised.

125
00:07:11,036 --> 00:07:14,546
It won't be long before
a Korean animation studio reaches the top.

126
00:07:14,549 --> 00:07:16,852
We should be part of that movement.

127
00:07:16,914 --> 00:07:18,485
I have to say...

128
00:07:19,626 --> 00:07:21,246
I really like what you're saying.

129
00:07:23,382 --> 00:07:25,167
For the houses in "The Three Little Pigs,"

130
00:07:26,208 --> 00:07:28,127
I'd like to depict their houses
as traditional Korean houses,

131
00:07:28,129 --> 00:07:31,160
a thatched house, a wooden house,
and a tiled-roof house.

132
00:07:31,407 --> 00:07:33,876
And for "The Seven Little Goats,"

133
00:07:34,186 --> 00:07:36,530
I think dressing them in hanbok
would be adorable.

134
00:07:36,586 --> 00:07:39,770
Good. You didn't have much time,
but you put a lot of thought into it.

135
00:07:39,832 --> 00:07:41,469
Lunch is on me.

136
00:07:43,895 --> 00:07:44,895
Yes.

137
00:07:45,921 --> 00:07:47,049
Excuse me.

138
00:07:58,792 --> 00:08:02,207
- Sir, lunch is here.
- Who ordered it?

139
00:08:02,570 --> 00:08:04,026
Did Lieutenant No order it?

140
00:08:05,062 --> 00:08:06,876
Well, not exactly.

141
00:08:07,512 --> 00:08:09,808
Ji Ni has a guardian angel.

142
00:08:10,010 --> 00:08:11,780
Someone who secretly looks after her.

143
00:08:12,144 --> 00:08:13,230
So you're dating someone.

144
00:08:13,232 --> 00:08:14,868
Yes.

145
00:08:15,129 --> 00:08:16,643
Go ahead and eat.

146
00:08:26,809 --> 00:08:29,832
That boyfriend of yours
sure knows how to take care of you.

147
00:08:37,910 --> 00:08:40,249
This is too much. Please stop.

148
00:08:40,291 --> 00:08:43,563
Come on. I can't just send it
once or twice and call it a day.

149
00:08:43,702 --> 00:08:46,140
- At least for a year.
- What?

150
00:08:47,045 --> 00:08:50,176
I'll make it a month. How's that?

151
00:08:50,253 --> 00:08:53,185
Enjoy your meal.
Stamina is a competitive edge.

152
00:08:53,323 --> 00:08:55,494
That's my favorite Korean saying.

153
00:08:55,496 --> 00:08:57,836
"Stamina is a competitive edge."
You got this!

154
00:09:08,851 --> 00:09:09,900
Excuse me.

155
00:09:10,351 --> 00:09:13,966
If you haven't had lunch yet,
why don't you join us?

156
00:09:23,841 --> 00:09:24,870
Well, this is something.

157
00:09:24,872 --> 00:09:27,710
Just from the sound,
it's like we're sitting by a waterfall.

158
00:09:30,704 --> 00:09:32,061
I'll enjoy the meal. Thanks.

159
00:09:32,270 --> 00:09:34,086
Thank your boyfriend for me.

160
00:09:34,194 --> 00:09:36,750
- And tell him to keep them coming.
- Sure.

161
00:09:54,641 --> 00:09:55,877
How should I put it?

162
00:09:56,890 --> 00:09:59,878
What's a polite verb
that still sounds like a strong request?

163
00:09:59,967 --> 00:10:01,130
Use a translator.

164
00:10:01,323 --> 00:10:04,627
It's not that I don't know the words.
I'm looking for the right one.

165
00:10:05,049 --> 00:10:06,847
The nuance changes depending
on the instrument, you know.

166
00:10:06,902 --> 00:10:08,392
True. They're all different.

167
00:10:08,812 --> 00:10:11,120
Wind and string instruments
are completely different.

168
00:10:11,563 --> 00:10:12,563
Here.

169
00:10:17,382 --> 00:10:18,716
You eat. I'll eat later.

170
00:10:18,860 --> 00:10:20,752
It's lunchtime. Have some manners.

171
00:10:20,830 --> 00:10:21,943
I'll be done soon.

172
00:10:23,718 --> 00:10:26,106
Couples never stay mad at each other.

173
00:10:26,443 --> 00:10:28,210
Look at them, feeding each other already.

174
00:10:29,944 --> 00:10:31,174
Must be nice.

175
00:10:37,718 --> 00:10:38,959
Why the sigh?

176
00:10:39,403 --> 00:10:41,206
You're back. How was the briefing?

177
00:10:41,756 --> 00:10:43,112
It went well.

178
00:10:43,769 --> 00:10:46,541
I'm exhausted. Get me a sweet coffee.

179
00:10:47,142 --> 00:10:48,379
Okay.

180
00:10:55,483 --> 00:10:58,510
They're cute together.
You're jealous, aren't you?

181
00:11:00,532 --> 00:11:03,416
- Aren't you jealous?
- Jealous of what?

182
00:11:03,650 --> 00:11:06,055
Just because I don't date
doesn't mean others shouldn't.

183
00:11:06,118 --> 00:11:08,180
Yeah. I'd rather they didn't either.

184
00:11:09,350 --> 00:11:12,822
Hey, for the sake of humanity,
tell everyone to date and get married.

185
00:11:13,079 --> 00:11:14,708
Just don't nag me about it.

186
00:11:25,820 --> 00:11:28,308
People who speak foreign languages
are so cool.

187
00:11:30,813 --> 00:11:33,367
Hey, put some ice in for me.

188
00:11:33,892 --> 00:11:35,529
I heard you didn't get into the center.

189
00:11:37,268 --> 00:11:39,738
- Jung A.
- Do Hee.

190
00:11:42,767 --> 00:11:44,901
I asked you to keep it a secret for now.

191
00:11:48,749 --> 00:11:49,842
Jung A.

192
00:11:51,870 --> 00:11:53,126
Jung A!

193
00:11:54,447 --> 00:11:55,682
How did you know?

194
00:11:55,963 --> 00:11:59,444
I saw it in your room.
It was in the announcement.

195
00:11:59,630 --> 00:12:00,876
Why was it a secret?

196
00:12:00,952 --> 00:12:02,980
Did she think she'd get in?

197
00:12:03,727 --> 00:12:05,806
With her skills, she's lucky
she even got into college.

198
00:12:06,043 --> 00:12:07,929
She drew much worse than I did
back in art school.

199
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:10,514
She asked me to wait until she was ready
to announce it herself.

200
00:12:10,612 --> 00:12:12,257
You embarrassed her by telling
everyone like this.

201
00:12:13,096 --> 00:12:15,184
Why make such a promise
in the first place?

202
00:12:15,530 --> 00:12:17,382
Don't worry about it.
She's just being dramatic.

203
00:12:18,950 --> 00:12:21,734
It's really no big deal. We're classmates.

204
00:12:21,790 --> 00:12:23,045
Can't we even talk about this?

205
00:12:34,060 --> 00:12:36,880
Honestly, it didn't really bother me
that much,

206
00:12:37,891 --> 00:12:41,570
but Do Hee suddenly saying it
like that made me feel embarrassed.

207
00:12:42,350 --> 00:12:44,447
You could've told me, though.

208
00:12:45,052 --> 00:12:47,335
I was going to check the website,
but you didn't say anything,

209
00:12:47,337 --> 00:12:48,707
so I waited.

210
00:12:50,998 --> 00:12:53,181
Until I was ready,

211
00:12:53,639 --> 00:12:56,095
I asked him to keep it a secret,

212
00:12:57,683 --> 00:12:59,555
but I guess there aren't many people
I can really trust.

213
00:13:01,718 --> 00:13:03,540
Do you want to stay here?

214
00:13:04,230 --> 00:13:05,709
Should I go wait at the café?

215
00:13:06,832 --> 00:13:08,126
I'll rest here for a bit.

216
00:13:08,552 --> 00:13:09,552
Okay.

217
00:13:09,849 --> 00:13:10,906
Get some rest.

218
00:13:19,919 --> 00:13:22,290
(Haemyeong University Hospital)

219
00:13:26,881 --> 00:13:30,489
The transplant resulted in successful
stem cell engraftment.

220
00:13:30,956 --> 00:13:33,519
His white blood cell count
has also risen steadily.

221
00:13:35,431 --> 00:13:36,482
Thank you.

222
00:13:37,382 --> 00:13:38,838
I'm grateful too.

223
00:13:39,857 --> 00:13:43,460
- No more getting sick, Cha O Reum.
- Say "Okay."

224
00:13:43,937 --> 00:13:45,672
He absolutely can't catch a cold.

225
00:13:45,967 --> 00:13:49,056
If you feel his fever rising a little,
come straight to the ER.

226
00:13:49,369 --> 00:13:52,875
- And watch out for mosquitoes.
- We'll take care of him like a newborn.

227
00:13:55,852 --> 00:13:57,959
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

228
00:13:58,047 --> 00:14:00,126
Take care. Goodbye.

229
00:14:02,148 --> 00:14:03,448
Okay, got it.

230
00:14:04,683 --> 00:14:05,878
That's great.

231
00:14:06,325 --> 00:14:08,439
I'll be right there after I meet someone.

232
00:14:19,012 --> 00:14:20,324
Are you shopping for your husband?

233
00:14:20,512 --> 00:14:21,829
How old is he?

234
00:14:22,902 --> 00:14:24,529
He's in his early fifties.

235
00:14:26,683 --> 00:14:28,332
Then how about this one?

236
00:14:29,028 --> 00:14:30,071
Yes.

237
00:14:35,083 --> 00:14:36,417
You're early.

238
00:14:36,710 --> 00:14:40,724
I picked out a few things beforehand.
I hope you like them.

239
00:14:40,790 --> 00:14:43,304
If you're buying them for me,
I'll wear whatever you choose.

240
00:14:45,730 --> 00:14:47,480
Can he try this on?

241
00:14:47,605 --> 00:14:49,224
Yes. This way.

242
00:14:50,313 --> 00:14:51,313
Okay.

243
00:14:59,855 --> 00:15:02,105
But isn't this a little too expensive?

244
00:15:03,063 --> 00:15:05,006
I picked out some cheaper ones too.

245
00:15:05,855 --> 00:15:07,605
Then just give me this one.

246
00:15:08,563 --> 00:15:11,061
I feel bad making you spend so much on me.

247
00:15:11,063 --> 00:15:13,480
It's okay.
I'm doing it because I'm grateful.

248
00:15:14,212 --> 00:15:15,769
O Reum is being discharged.

249
00:15:16,021 --> 00:15:17,227
Really?

250
00:15:17,511 --> 00:15:19,731
I'm so happy that he's being discharged,
so I wanted to buy you something.

251
00:15:21,938 --> 00:15:23,363
Congratulations.

252
00:15:28,001 --> 00:15:30,349
Don't call me "Teacher" when we're out.

253
00:15:30,438 --> 00:15:32,843
People seem to get the wrong idea
about me.

254
00:15:32,980 --> 00:15:34,355
Then what should I call you?

255
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:36,688
Call me by my name.
I call you Sa Bin too.

256
00:15:36,855 --> 00:15:38,313
Okay, Yeong Ju.

257
00:15:40,033 --> 00:15:42,283
Is that why the sales clerk kept staring?

258
00:15:43,021 --> 00:15:44,163
You noticed?

259
00:15:44,938 --> 00:15:45,938
Well...

260
00:15:46,313 --> 00:15:49,230
He probably thought I was
a returning student dating a professor.

261
00:15:54,521 --> 00:15:56,227
Why do I keep getting calls?

262
00:15:56,230 --> 00:15:57,271
You should answer.

263
00:15:57,605 --> 00:15:59,133
Excuse me for a moment.

264
00:16:00,188 --> 00:16:01,188
Hello?

265
00:16:01,563 --> 00:16:03,646
I told you I'm not going.
Why do you keep asking?

266
00:16:04,521 --> 00:16:06,103
What does the alumni reunion
have to do with me?

267
00:16:06,105 --> 00:16:07,813
I've never even gone to one.

268
00:16:08,563 --> 00:16:09,605
Fine, I got it.

269
00:16:09,980 --> 00:16:11,953
I'm meeting someone right now.

270
00:16:11,980 --> 00:16:14,232
Yeah, I'll think about it.

271
00:16:16,188 --> 00:16:17,868
Is the reunion for college?

272
00:16:17,980 --> 00:16:19,563
No, high school.

273
00:16:20,146 --> 00:16:23,370
It's the 50th anniversary this year,
so I guess they're making it a big event.

274
00:16:23,688 --> 00:16:25,605
I was in the broadcasting club,

275
00:16:25,688 --> 00:16:28,403
so they're asking me to attend
the broadcasting club homecoming.

276
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:30,853
You should go.
Which high school did you attend?

277
00:16:30,855 --> 00:16:32,061
Ilyeong Girls' High School.

278
00:16:32,063 --> 00:16:33,811
Ilyeong Girls' High School?

279
00:16:33,813 --> 00:16:35,813
My sister-in-law went there too.

280
00:16:35,980 --> 00:16:37,611
- It's in Nam Mi Dong.
- That's right.

281
00:16:38,938 --> 00:16:40,490
What a coincidence.

282
00:16:41,271 --> 00:16:42,450
Which graduating class?

283
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:45,240
I don't remember.

284
00:16:45,396 --> 00:16:48,729
I got married young, so I didn't
have much time to keep up with friends.

285
00:16:49,271 --> 00:16:52,313
After I was on my own,
I went out even less.

286
00:16:52,855 --> 00:16:53,896
You should go.

287
00:16:54,230 --> 00:16:56,728
My sister-in-law is probably
on the reunion committee.

288
00:16:56,730 --> 00:16:58,074
I'll mention it to her.

289
00:16:58,563 --> 00:16:59,644
No, it's okay.

290
00:16:59,646 --> 00:17:02,452
Once O Reum is discharged,
I probably won't have any time anyway.

291
00:17:04,230 --> 00:17:05,230
Right.

292
00:17:05,855 --> 00:17:09,247
You've spent all this time
just being a mother and a grandmother.

293
00:17:11,230 --> 00:17:12,521
Well...

294
00:17:13,813 --> 00:17:15,105
I suppose that's true.

295
00:17:15,438 --> 00:17:18,105
Men do the same, don't they?
They're just dads and grandfathers.

296
00:17:18,313 --> 00:17:20,340
Yes, that's true, but...

297
00:17:21,563 --> 00:17:22,728
still,

298
00:17:22,730 --> 00:17:25,410
don't you think your youth is too short?

299
00:17:26,021 --> 00:17:27,313
I suppose so.

300
00:17:29,563 --> 00:17:31,923
My youth was pretty short.

301
00:17:32,146 --> 00:17:34,929
You did get married young.

302
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:38,165
Yes. I got pregnant with Seung Hyun,
so we got married.

303
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:41,282
That's why my oldest son feels guilty
about it.

304
00:17:41,896 --> 00:17:43,464
He thinks I got tied down...

305
00:17:43,605 --> 00:17:45,438
because of him.

306
00:17:47,021 --> 00:17:48,758
Do you feel that way too?

307
00:17:48,813 --> 00:17:49,980
No.

308
00:17:50,693 --> 00:17:52,560
We got married
because we loved each other.

309
00:17:52,563 --> 00:17:53,688
Isn't that only natural?

310
00:17:53,938 --> 00:17:55,944
It's a shame he passed away.

311
00:17:56,146 --> 00:17:58,396
Leaving behind such a beautiful wife
and sons.

312
00:17:58,896 --> 00:18:00,646
If it were me, I could never have left.

313
00:18:01,021 --> 00:18:03,325
How can you fight fate?

314
00:18:05,105 --> 00:18:06,353
Yeong Ju.

315
00:18:06,355 --> 00:18:07,521
Is there nothing you want to do?

316
00:18:07,896 --> 00:18:08,938
All of a sudden,

317
00:18:09,063 --> 00:18:11,771
I want to help you
rediscover yourself as a woman.

318
00:18:12,688 --> 00:18:14,503
Where is she? Where?

319
00:18:16,021 --> 00:18:17,535
I appreciate the thought.

320
00:18:17,605 --> 00:18:18,936
O Reum is getting discharged today,

321
00:18:18,938 --> 00:18:20,936
so I have to go home and be a grandma.

322
00:18:20,938 --> 00:18:22,396
Really?

323
00:18:23,230 --> 00:18:25,728
I can't exactly ask you to stay
if O Reum is being discharged.

324
00:18:25,730 --> 00:18:26,978
Of course.

325
00:18:26,980 --> 00:18:29,040
Our whole family has been waiting
for this day.

326
00:18:30,595 --> 00:18:31,687
Thank you...

327
00:18:32,021 --> 00:18:33,182
so much.

328
00:18:33,896 --> 00:18:35,907
I feel like I've made a friend.

329
00:18:36,688 --> 00:18:39,406
After I got married, I grew distant
from my classmates and my family...

330
00:18:39,688 --> 00:18:41,105
from everyone.

331
00:18:42,450 --> 00:18:44,116
I'll go to the reunion with you.

332
00:18:44,930 --> 00:18:46,305
If partners are allowed.

333
00:18:47,521 --> 00:18:49,783
Shall we? I think that'd be nice.

334
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:53,103
The friends who thought I'd stay a widow
for the rest of my life...

335
00:18:53,105 --> 00:18:54,890
will be in for quite a surprise.

336
00:18:55,521 --> 00:18:57,019
Let's take walks in the park sometimes.

337
00:18:57,021 --> 00:18:58,353
Summer nights are nice.

338
00:18:58,355 --> 00:19:00,551
Yes, let's go...

339
00:19:00,605 --> 00:19:01,778
to Nam San again.

340
00:19:02,896 --> 00:19:04,146
This time,

341
00:19:04,313 --> 00:19:05,932
let's smile instead of crying.

342
00:19:07,406 --> 00:19:08,406
Really?

343
00:19:09,063 --> 00:19:10,063
Promise me.

344
00:19:12,146 --> 00:19:13,605
- I promise.
- Seal it.

345
00:19:13,855 --> 00:19:14,894
Sealed.

346
00:19:14,896 --> 00:19:16,480
High five.

347
00:19:20,355 --> 00:19:21,938
We can't get anything right.

348
00:19:26,771 --> 00:19:28,061
Welcome.

349
00:19:28,063 --> 00:19:29,980
- Just a cup of tea, please.
- Okay.

350
00:19:30,271 --> 00:19:31,603
Have you been waiting long?

351
00:19:31,886 --> 00:19:33,041
No, just a little.

352
00:19:33,355 --> 00:19:35,646
It's my fault for showing up unannounced.

353
00:19:35,730 --> 00:19:37,260
I just assumed you'd be here.

354
00:19:37,896 --> 00:19:39,728
I only work mornings once a week.

355
00:19:39,730 --> 00:19:41,771
- I need a break too.
- Of course.

356
00:19:42,146 --> 00:19:44,489
Sa Bin, I heard you own this building.

357
00:19:49,688 --> 00:19:50,979
Was it a secret?

358
00:19:51,021 --> 00:19:52,728
I didn't know. I...

359
00:19:52,730 --> 00:19:55,063
bragged that the rent issue
had been completely sorted out.

360
00:19:55,146 --> 00:19:56,728
She was really worried about it.

361
00:19:56,730 --> 00:19:59,603
It's no secret. My sister-in-law
was managing it before...

362
00:19:59,605 --> 00:20:01,813
and I simply took it back. It's okay.

363
00:20:02,396 --> 00:20:03,938
I was afraid I'd made another mistake.

364
00:20:06,688 --> 00:20:08,015
I'll let you talk.

365
00:20:10,396 --> 00:20:12,688
When I receive the money from Indonesia,

366
00:20:13,063 --> 00:20:15,061
I'll buy a building like this
and rent it out.

367
00:20:15,063 --> 00:20:16,396
I could teach cello there too.

368
00:20:16,399 --> 00:20:17,720
That's a good idea.

369
00:20:17,931 --> 00:20:19,452
Should I find one for you?

370
00:20:19,521 --> 00:20:20,853
Actually,

371
00:20:20,855 --> 00:20:23,061
my sister-in-law knows a lot about this.

372
00:20:23,063 --> 00:20:25,646
Yes, please. We can discuss it
once the money comes in.

373
00:20:25,813 --> 00:20:26,813
Okay.

374
00:20:31,271 --> 00:20:33,744
Have you been sick? You look rather pale.

375
00:20:34,105 --> 00:20:36,477
I can't fool a Korean medicine doctor.

376
00:20:36,855 --> 00:20:38,436
I tried to kill myself.

377
00:20:38,438 --> 00:20:39,438
Why would you do that?

378
00:20:39,563 --> 00:20:41,269
I wanted to get back at my daughter
for what she did.

379
00:20:41,271 --> 00:20:42,330
My Musician.

380
00:20:43,021 --> 00:20:46,130
Why are you so shocked?
I've always wanted to die.

381
00:20:48,188 --> 00:20:49,938
When we drank together last time...

382
00:20:50,206 --> 00:20:51,206
Yes.

383
00:20:51,938 --> 00:20:54,603
I told her over and over not to do it,

384
00:20:54,605 --> 00:20:56,146
but she deceived me and did it anyway.

385
00:20:56,188 --> 00:20:58,811
I thought, "If I'm going to live
with this kind of disrespect,

386
00:20:58,813 --> 00:21:01,477
I might as well leave for good."

387
00:21:02,197 --> 00:21:03,537
But...

388
00:21:05,230 --> 00:21:08,244
can't you tell me what happened?

389
00:21:08,730 --> 00:21:11,617
I couldn't understand a thing
you said last time either.

390
00:21:11,730 --> 00:21:13,269
It's complicated.

391
00:21:13,271 --> 00:21:14,271
I see.

392
00:21:22,313 --> 00:21:24,480
O Reum, Grandma's here.

393
00:21:25,063 --> 00:21:26,605
- Surprise!
- Grandma.

394
00:21:26,646 --> 00:21:27,978
My darling.

395
00:21:27,980 --> 00:21:29,188
Stop.

396
00:21:30,168 --> 00:21:32,521
Mother, please wash your hands first,

397
00:21:32,549 --> 00:21:35,299
and change your clothes
before holding O Reum.

398
00:21:35,438 --> 00:21:37,271
No hugs while wearing outdoor clothes.

399
00:21:39,063 --> 00:21:40,105
Sorry.

400
00:21:40,396 --> 00:21:43,146
The doctor said O Reum
hasn't fully recovered yet.

401
00:21:44,730 --> 00:21:45,730
Okay.

402
00:21:45,938 --> 00:21:47,105
I guess it can't be helped.

403
00:21:47,521 --> 00:21:49,686
O Reum, Grandma is going to wash up.

404
00:21:49,688 --> 00:21:50,813
Then we can have a hug, okay?

405
00:21:59,188 --> 00:22:02,027
That dramatic couple
is being even more dramatic now.

406
00:22:02,855 --> 00:22:04,063
There's nothing we can do.

407
00:22:09,184 --> 00:22:10,184
Again?

408
00:22:10,313 --> 00:22:11,313
Mom.

409
00:22:14,355 --> 00:22:15,959
Mother, dinner's ready.

410
00:22:19,605 --> 00:22:21,172
I'll leave a knife there from now on.

411
00:22:21,188 --> 00:22:23,438
They said O Reum became ill
because we didn't put one there.

412
00:22:23,813 --> 00:22:25,290
- Mai, that's...
- Fine.

413
00:22:25,771 --> 00:22:27,167
Do whatever you want.

414
00:22:27,605 --> 00:22:30,561
That's pretty cool of you, Mother.

415
00:22:30,563 --> 00:22:31,728
What else can I do?

416
00:22:31,896 --> 00:22:34,687
We should try anything
that might help O Reum.

417
00:22:38,480 --> 00:22:39,818
Mom, let's go too.

418
00:22:43,980 --> 00:22:45,438
My precious baby.

419
00:22:50,688 --> 00:22:52,058
Thank you, O Reum...

420
00:22:52,850 --> 00:22:54,726
for coming back to us.

421
00:22:55,105 --> 00:22:57,487
Thank you so much, my darling.

422
00:23:05,855 --> 00:23:08,138
I kept hugging him too.

423
00:23:08,355 --> 00:23:09,521
Ji Ni...

424
00:23:09,855 --> 00:23:11,286
I'm so grateful to her.

425
00:23:11,396 --> 00:23:12,521
I'm truly thankful.

426
00:23:12,646 --> 00:23:14,390
I sent her lunch today too.

427
00:23:14,605 --> 00:23:16,271
I'm just so grateful to her.

428
00:23:34,188 --> 00:23:35,538
Uncle, did you buy new clothes?

429
00:23:35,980 --> 00:23:37,311
Someone bought them for me.

430
00:23:37,313 --> 00:23:38,313
Who?

431
00:23:38,556 --> 00:23:39,561
Don't tell me it was a woman.

432
00:23:39,563 --> 00:23:41,727
You're not the only one
who gets shirts from women.

433
00:23:41,730 --> 00:23:43,197
There's a woman who buys me things too.

434
00:23:43,230 --> 00:23:44,269
Are you seeing someone?

435
00:23:44,271 --> 00:23:46,063
Are you looking down on me?

436
00:23:46,563 --> 00:23:48,311
You punk. Your eyes are about to pop out.

437
00:23:48,313 --> 00:23:49,521
You really surprised me.

438
00:23:51,021 --> 00:23:52,398
Does father know this wonderful news?

439
00:23:52,730 --> 00:23:55,197
Don't tell him about this.

440
00:23:55,313 --> 00:23:57,853
It isn't the relationship you think it is.

441
00:23:57,855 --> 00:23:59,051
What do you mean, it's not?

442
00:23:59,146 --> 00:24:01,313
If she buys you clothes,
father should know about it.

443
00:24:02,188 --> 00:24:05,186
You've got it wrong.
Her grandson recently had leukemia,

444
00:24:05,188 --> 00:24:07,269
so I made him some medicine for the pain
and helped him out.

445
00:24:07,271 --> 00:24:10,186
So she gave me these clothes
as a thank-you gift.

446
00:24:10,188 --> 00:24:11,313
Her grandson?

447
00:24:11,688 --> 00:24:12,688
Is she a grandmother?

448
00:24:13,008 --> 00:24:14,383
She doesn't look like one.

449
00:24:14,605 --> 00:24:15,938
She's really cute.

450
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:18,794
What a disappointment.

451
00:24:18,938 --> 00:24:20,186
I said she doesn't look like one.

452
00:24:20,188 --> 00:24:21,652
But she's still a grandmother.

453
00:24:21,813 --> 00:24:23,636
But how did her grandson recover
from leukemia?

454
00:24:23,688 --> 00:24:24,728
I know someone who...

455
00:24:24,730 --> 00:24:26,787
donated bone marrow
to a child with leukemia.

456
00:24:27,438 --> 00:24:28,828
And the relationship between them was...

457
00:24:30,813 --> 00:24:33,063
Forget it. That's personal information.

458
00:24:33,688 --> 00:24:35,230
The world is full of good people.

459
00:24:35,789 --> 00:24:38,144
If she's a grandmother,
is there a grandfather too?

460
00:24:38,146 --> 00:24:40,247
No. She's been alone for many years.

461
00:24:40,480 --> 00:24:42,563
Anyway, that's all.
Don't get too interested.

462
00:24:42,646 --> 00:24:44,438
I was interested for a moment.

463
00:24:45,063 --> 00:24:46,641
That was disappointing.

464
00:24:48,230 --> 00:24:51,102
Why are you making such a fuss
over your own disappointment?

465
00:25:21,355 --> 00:25:25,480
The phone you're calling is turned off.
You'll be connected to voicemail.

466
00:25:26,896 --> 00:25:28,809
That little brat...

467
00:25:38,271 --> 00:25:40,521
(Dear Mother)

468
00:25:41,021 --> 00:25:42,480
What should I do? It's your mother.

469
00:25:43,438 --> 00:25:45,528
Don't answer it. You'd better not.

470
00:25:45,771 --> 00:25:47,686
I'll be home very late tonight.

471
00:25:47,688 --> 00:25:49,063
(Dear Mother)

472
00:25:55,271 --> 00:25:57,521
That little brat is doing this on purpose.

473
00:26:02,355 --> 00:26:03,480
Mother, I'm sorry.

474
00:26:03,521 --> 00:26:04,855
I'm Ji Ni's friend...

475
00:26:05,605 --> 00:26:06,938
not yours, Mother.

476
00:26:22,105 --> 00:26:23,105
Okay.

477
00:26:23,396 --> 00:26:25,438
I need to stay hydrated for my health.

478
00:26:27,021 --> 00:26:28,230
Honey, aren't you proud of me?

479
00:26:29,396 --> 00:26:31,491
I'll follow our daughter's advice for now.

480
00:26:41,896 --> 00:26:44,168
Attorney, I'm still waiting for your call.

481
00:26:47,938 --> 00:26:51,099
Let's see
if this month's interest payment went out.

482
00:27:00,896 --> 00:27:01,938
Zero dollars?

483
00:27:03,230 --> 00:27:04,480
How can this be?

484
00:27:05,480 --> 00:27:06,521
Hold on.

485
00:27:08,021 --> 00:27:09,855
(Cha Production, Na Se Ri,
current balance, zero dollars)

486
00:27:17,396 --> 00:27:21,688
The phone you're calling is turned off.
You'll be connected to voicemail.

487
00:27:30,438 --> 00:27:32,269
How can the company's balance be zero?

488
00:27:32,271 --> 00:27:34,103
What's going on? Is this an error?

489
00:27:34,105 --> 00:27:36,481
Is the system down?

490
00:28:03,188 --> 00:28:06,478
(Family Register)

491
00:28:06,480 --> 00:28:08,519
I think I've been scammed.

492
00:28:08,521 --> 00:28:09,980
This is unbelievable.

493
00:28:10,063 --> 00:28:11,353
Mom, have you always been this reckless?

494
00:28:11,355 --> 00:28:13,103
If she even knows your high school,
you two must be pretty close.

495
00:28:13,105 --> 00:28:14,561
Uncle, you have a weakness
for people who sing well.

496
00:28:14,563 --> 00:28:15,686
That's true.

497
00:28:15,688 --> 00:28:17,644
This is just wrong.

498
00:28:17,646 --> 00:28:18,936
Is your taste really this bad?

499
00:28:18,938 --> 00:28:21,487
Never introduce someone
before you're ready to marry them.

500
00:28:21,490 --> 00:28:22,519
Mom!

501
00:28:22,521 --> 00:28:23,771
Do you know what this house means to me?

502
00:28:23,855 --> 00:28:25,646
How could you make me leave it?

503
00:28:27,978 --> 00:28:29,978
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
